  "provider_query": "Wall Street Journal article page about the 2024 Nobel Prize in Physics",
  "answer": "The 2024 Nobel Prize in Physics went to John J. Hopfield and Geoffrey E. Hinton for foundational work on artificial neural networks and machine learning. Relevant Wall Street Journal pages:\n\n1. **AI Pioneers John Hopfield and Geoffrey Hinton Win Nobel Prize in Physics** (main article)  \n   Aylin Woodward, updated Oct. 8, 2024. Covers the award for inventions enabling machine learning with neural networks that underpin modern AI.  \n   https://www.wsj.com/science/nobel-prize-in-physics-awarded-to-duo-for-machine-learning-c9e4b0d7\n\n2. **A Godfather of AI Just Won a Nobel. He Has Been Warning the Machines Could Take Over the World.**  \n   Updated Oct. 9, 2024. Follow-up on Hinton’s safety warnings after sharing the physics prize with Hopfield.  \n   https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/a-godfather-of-ai-just-won-a-nobel-he-has-been-warning-the-machines-could-take-over-the-world-b127da71\n\n3. **Nobel Prize in Chemistry Awarded to Trio Who Used AI to Crack the Code of Proteins**  \n   Brianna Abbott, updated Oct. 9, 2024. Notes the physics prize the day before to Hopfield and Hinton for machine-learning foundations.  \n   https://www.wsj.com/science/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-awarded-to-trio-for-cracking-code-to-predict-protein-structure-62295a7d\n\n4. **WSJ newspaper PDF (Oct. 9, 2024)** — print coverage of the Hopfield–Hinton physics prize and neural-network work.  \n   https://www.wsj.com/public/resources/documents/LKm4CO40tO1rZUvD4vDr-WSJNewsPaper-10-9-2024.pdf\n\n5. **WSJ newspaper PDF (Oct. 10, 2024)** — further print coverage of Hinton’s Nobel and AI-risk comments, plus the chemistry prize.  \n   https://www.wsj.com/public/resources/documents/U9AKwHSdzNii9VLVoe2o-WSJNewsPaper-10-10-2024.pdf\n\n6. **Chinese WSJ version of the Hinton follow-up** (“AI教父”辛顿获得诺贝尔奖…)  \n   Oct. 10, 2024. Same story as item 2, in Chinese.  \n   https://cn.wsj.com/articles/ai教父-辛顿获得诺贝尔奖-近年来一直警告机器可能统治世界-c91993cc\n\nPrimary page for the award announcement is result 1.",
